1
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:14,180
I'm on a journey out to see the world.

2
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,160
While I'm on my own, I've
yet to reach the end.

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,840
So won't you come along with me right now?

4
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:23,777
Surely then we can!

5
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,780
Follow me now as we
journey on from sea to sea.

6
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:32,220
For that treasure known
by everybody as one piece.

7
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:37,440
Even though they laugh and
say it's just a fantasy.

8
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,857
We are going, there's no doubt we go.

9
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:45,180
Cause we can feel the
rush of energy overcome.

10
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,280
It will lead the way.

11
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,480
Keep pretending that you know what to do.

12
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:57,397
Books will only get in the way.

13
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:00,000
No guides for today.

14
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:03,977
Do not worry soon, the rain
will be gone with the wind.

15
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:06,597
Keep your chin up, raise the
anchor, now that's what you'll do.

16
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:09,297
Give it time and calm the storm
that you have built within.

17
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,417
Come and have my board at number two.

18
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:14,777
Once tomorrow's wind picks up,
we set self cause we can't.

19
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:17,297
Thresh enough, stand tall and
take a look at one of you.

20
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:19,657
All the journey makes
me wanna see somebody.

21
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,681
There are things out there
you just won't believe.

22
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,720
Beyond your wildest dreams.

23
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:30,780
Don't think for a second,
it's not the truth.

24
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,800
That's the story most will believe.

25
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:37,440
Not me, come and see.

26
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,777
I am on a journey out to sea.

27
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:43,297
The world done on my own.

28
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:45,337
I've got my group of friends.

29
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:47,357
Together we've got our way.

30
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,957
That's how it's done.

31
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,017
Says your captain.

32
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,277
Who says it can't be done?

33
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,937
We haven't even tried.

34
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:55,937
Gotta just believe we'll
make it to the end.

35
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,577
I just wanna do it all right now.

36
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,837
Together surely we can.

37
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,717
Yes, we can.

38
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,117
You can.

39
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:06,737
Just take this moment in.

40
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:08,057
We can.

41
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:09,437
I can.

42
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,157
Just take this feeling in.

43
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,477
Right now.

44
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:14,900
Right now.

45
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:18,740
Oh yes, we can.

46
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,077
Yes, we can!

47
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:26,990
Yes, we can!

48
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:36,970
Wha...

49
00:02:37,053 --> 00:02:38,300
What is this?

50
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,040
How'd this happen? Hey!

51
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,052
Hey, where is everybody?

52
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,140
Who did this to Zoe?

53
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:52,716
I'll make whoever's behind this pain.

54
00:02:55,880 --> 00:03:00,645
Don't tell me it was those depraved,
straw-hot virus behind all this destruction.

55
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,180
What the hell did they do to my home?

56
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:25,137
This fortress was a living space
once inhabited by our ancestors.

57
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:27,100
Since ancient times,

58
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:30,877
Zunesha has carried the entire
history of the Mink tribe on its back.

59
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:35,360
One of our most cherished traditions
has been passed down for generations.

60
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:40,002
The trading of clothes with an
outsider is a symbol of friendship.

61
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,860
Wow, how gorgeous!

62
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:43,897
Must belong to someone important, huh?

63
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:45,920
Indeed so.

64
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:47,691
It's a national treasure.

65
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,520
And it's for me?

66
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:52,730
Of course.

67
00:03:52,813 --> 00:03:54,420
We insist that you have it.

68
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:56,470
Crush!

69
00:03:56,553 --> 00:03:57,460
Garchu-chu!

70
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,000
Mademoiselle, Crush.

71
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,540
Why, Crush?

72
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:06,420
How about you? Crush.

73
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:08,000
Crush, sir?

74
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,630
Tristan!

75
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:13,630
Crush!

76
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,917
Crush! Crush!

77
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,412
You two, you sure like our greeting, huh?

78
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:20,990
Oh!

79
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,510
Crush!

80
00:04:24,593 --> 00:04:26,740
What a miraculous magic word!

81
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:29,274
Even though I don't know what it means!

82
00:04:29,820 --> 00:04:30,920
Sanji here!

83
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:34,800
We want to do a round of Crush
with our savior! Piss off!

84
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,240
It's ladies only!

85
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:37,678
Hello there, Sanji!

86
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:39,130
Crush!

87
00:04:39,213 --> 00:04:41,660
Viva l 'amintimusia!

88
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:44,460
A goddess?

89
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:45,830
No!

90
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,550
Mommy!

91
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,020
Don't you!

92
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,180
Maybe not!

93
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:58,220
Where's Momo?

94
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,980
He's locked himself away in his room.

95
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,100
He was suffering from anxiety.

96
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,680
Besides, it's better if he's incognito.

97
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:07,797
That's a good point.

98
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:11,939
While we're at it, we should avoid
the word samurai while we're here.

99
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:17,297
Well, if it were up to me, I'd
hand the brat over to the minx.

100
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:20,040
And ditch this dumb
island already. Shut up!

101
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,871
What's the update on the medicine, Caesar?

102
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:25,697
Naturally, I met the
quota since I'm a genius.

103
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:26,720
Stop slacking!

104
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:29,677
There's still a great deal
of people in need of help.

105
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:30,590
Make more.

106
00:05:30,673 --> 00:05:32,892
I think we have more than enough, though.

107
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:33,950
Dr.

108
00:05:34,033 --> 00:05:36,171
Caesar, I've come to pick up the medicine.

109
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:40,957
You must have me mixed
up with someone else.

110
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:43,020
I'm Cedar the pharmacist. Here.

111
00:05:44,340 --> 00:05:47,458
Damn, why do I have to make
this crap to help people?

112
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:49,960
Thank you, Tia. Dr. Caesar.

113
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,260
It's Cedar!

114
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:56,426
Man, I'm supposed to be Caesar the genius
mad scientist, not the charity worker.

115
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:58,660
Oh, almost forgot. Call me Cedar!

116
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,060
Heya, Baron Corpse.

117
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:01,965
Some fans are waiting outside.

118
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:05,260
I know they only want me for my bones.

119
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:06,931
Let's not entertain that.

120
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:10,840
Hey, Peckholms, good to see you, Conney.

121
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:14,100
It's been a while. Welcome back.

122
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:19,200
I'm so happy to see you're all okay.

123
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:24,557
Dad, Mom, my friends and
family, you're all alive.

124
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,000
It's been way too long.

125
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:29,340
Hey, Peckholms, this
brings back good memories.

126
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:32,444
It's so wonderful to have
you, Conney, back home.

127
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:33,610
Got you.

128
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,340
You idiot!

129
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:41,080
How can you be so happy when
you're covered in cuts and bruises?

130
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:45,900
My heart nearly stopped when I saw the
state that the city was in! Ease up!

131
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,256
That hurts, Pickles!

132
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:53,306
It's all thanks to the Straw Hat
Pirates that were still alive.

133
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:56,077
If it weren't for their
compassion and quick action,

134
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:59,336
I'm afraid to think of what
would have happened to us.

135
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,457
I'm so glad.

136
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:04,340
Thank you for hanging in there for me.

137
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,140
Come on, stop crying!

138
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,117
Dammit, I will never forgive.

139
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:17,137
Junk of the Beast Pirates
for as long as I live!

140
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:20,520
How dare he terrorize my innocent old lad?

141
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:25,297
That's them, they're
from the Big Mom Pirates.

142
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:26,837
They must have tailed us.

143
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:28,257
That's Peckham's down there!

144
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:29,840
He finally came back.

145
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,454
That kid was a troublemaker growing up.

146
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:34,780
So he's a mint?

147
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,981
Guess that makes sense, actually.

148
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:40,577
They must have overheard
where we were heading.

149
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:41,954
They're coming for me!

150
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:47,252
Whatever you do, please don't
hand me over, pretty please.

151
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,677
Don't forget that you are our trump
card for dealing with Doflamingo.

152
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:55,377
Now that Luffy and the others have beaten
him, we don't have a use for you anymore.

153
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:57,337
Now how could you say that to me?

154
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,000
We're bros, aren't we?

155
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:00,880
When did we become bros?

156
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:05,060
So, what the hell did you do to
piss off Big Mom? Spit it out.

157
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:06,857
I know you're hiding something from us.

158
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:08,800
Look, just hear me out, okay?

159
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:11,677
I accepted a grant for
research from Big Mom,

160
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,557
and I haven't quite gotten
anywhere with it yet,

161
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:15,816
so I lied and pocketed all the money.

162
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:16,940
Can you blame me?

163
00:08:17,100 --> 00:08:20,997
Doe Flamingo had my back at the time,
so I may have gotten a bit carried away.

164
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:22,727
Sounds like you earned this.

165
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:26,435
If they're just looking for
Caesar, that's no big deal.

166
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:29,320
Once I get there,

167
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:35,240
I'm gonna kick your ass, and then
I'll make Fishman Island my territory!

168
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:40,798
Although that may not be the case,
Luffy did pick a fight with Big Mom.

169
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:43,357
We busted up their ship pretty good, too.

170
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:49,160
Listen, Blackleg, how about we work
together and take out the goons?

171
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,785
Nami, stay here with everyone.

172
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:03,160
And Brooke, you come with me. Understood.

173
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:06,797
Are you still considering my
brilliant assassination proposition?

174
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:09,645
I'm not looking for
suggestions from dumbasses.

175
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:24,690
AHHHHH!

176
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:28,000
Alright you guys, what
exactly do you want?

177
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:32,897
The people of this land have had their
fair share of suffering recently.

178
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,680
I'd rather not add to
their list of traumas.

179
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:38,100
Can we try to talk things over first?

180
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:46,360
I just wanted to say thank you so much!

181
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,360
Enough already.

182
00:09:57,280 --> 00:10:01,837
I never expected to come back home and
see it completely devastated like this.

183
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,750
Get out!

184
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:07,577
But you and your crew may
selflessly save my people.

185
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:09,780
You're the reason they're alive!

186
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:12,120
How could I ever repay you?

187
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:22,240
Mama gave two orders.

188
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:26,457
First was to capture Caesar, but this
second one won't be too pleasant.

189
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:30,187
It might even mean the end of
the road for the Straw Hat crew.

190
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,280
That's ominous.

191
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:32,680
So I'm calling it!

192
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,197
The mission isn't failure.

193
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,574
Just hand over Caesar!

194
00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:40,396
I'll explain to mama that we let the
Stryhats get away this time, okay?

195
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:45,852
You gotta choke those feelings down,
kid, if you knows what's good for you.

196
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:47,469
Shut the hell up, new guy!

197
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:49,424
I'm gonna take the fall for it!

198
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,832
You don't understand the position I'm in.

199
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:58,707
I can't do anything to the people who
saved the lives of my friends and family.

200
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,620
Yellow-bellied rat.

201
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:16,380
Oh, damn you.

202
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:24,860
Why'd he shoot him? They're allies.

203
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:26,960
What a monster.

204
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:34,120
Was that real? Can't be.

205
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:39,080
He don't look it, but he's
got quite the rap sheet.

206
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:45,346
Unfortunately, he decided to act on his
stupid feelings, and now he's gone soft.

207
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,880
Yeah, he ain't no good to me now.

208
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:52,320
I'll finish the job.

209
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:55,140
Look alive, boys.

210
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:56,420
Do your stuff.

211
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:09,380
Go!

212
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,360
No!

213
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:44,220
What's going on?

214
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,720
You're outnumbered.

215
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,567
You might as well surrender.

216
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,900
Where did they come from?

217
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:01,680
His gut?

218
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:04,100
How messed up is that? Indeed.

219
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,127
I saw those men in his hand.

220
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:07,920
But I thought I imagined it.

221
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:11,400
That's on account of
the castle castle fruit.

222
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:13,440
Your captain and I,

223
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:17,077
we're both considered to be part
of the same generation of pirates.

224
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:18,320
This guy knows me.

225
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:19,700
Don't you, pal?

226
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:23,653
When Luffy clocked that
celestial dragon back at Sabaody,

227
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:27,292
you were there with the rest
of the worst generation, huh?

228
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,412
But we ain't trying to make a scene here.

229
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,447
Let's keep this thing quiet.

230
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:35,267
That's better for everybody.

231
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:40,757
If any of the minks show up, then it's a
pretty good bet they'll take your side.

232
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:44,134
And believe you me, those
cats really know how to scrap.

233
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:45,570
Vino!

234
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:48,700
Hey, cut that out! Let us go!

235
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,220
Nami! Chopper!

236
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:56,000
Sorry, guys.

237
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:58,104
We were getting really curious.

238
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:00,789
And we thought there
were only two of them.

239
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:07,840
Hey, Caesar!

240
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,720
You can come out now!

241
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:16,197
Or we can fill you full
of holes with these

242
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:19,045
sea prism stone bullets
in about three seconds.

243
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:20,450
Three...

244
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:24,470
Two...

245
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:26,100
Light him up!

246
00:14:27,500 --> 00:14:29,340
Wait, here I come! Don't shoot!

247
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:37,100
Don't point those at me!

248
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:41,660
Actually, it occurs to me we
ain't got no sea prism stone ammo.

249
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:42,760
How dare you?

250
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,200
What we do have is a spear
that'll work the same way.

251
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:50,500
I think we ought to continue this
conversation inside my castle.

252
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,100
That's an order.

253
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,700
I ain't got all day.

254
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:58,690
Great.

255
00:14:58,773 --> 00:15:00,520
This bastard's calling all the shots.

256
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,600
So we were forced to enter.

257
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,600
THE END

258
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,580
Sorry to make you wait

259
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:50,580
Is anybody hungry?

260
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:51,857
Don't be shy.

261
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:53,677
Not interested.

262
